On Sun, Apr 19, 2015 at 4:09 PM, John Cowan <cowan@mercury.ccil.org> wrote:

> Jorge Llamb=C3=ADas scripsit:
>
> > The apostrophe fix is more "lojbanic". in the sense that it uses forms
> that
> > already exist in lujvo instead of forms exclusive to fu'ivla/cmevla, so
> the
> > resulting words look more like core lojban words. But, as you say, it
> > doesn't always work.
>
> It can fail if the prefix is CVC or non-existent, but always works with
> 4-letter prefixes.  The only constraint then is "starts with a consonant,
> ends with a vowel".
>

I think it always works with a CVC prefix too. Type-3 always have a
consonantal syllable, so they can never be confused with lujvo, which never
have consonantal syllables. So yes, it's type-4s where it sometimes fails,
because the apostrophe may create either a lujvo or a slinku'i.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

